```javascript
// Function to sort a JSON object by keys in ascending order
function sortJsonObjectByKeys(jsonObj) {
  // Convert the JSON object into an array of key-value pairs
  const entries = Object.entries(jsonObj);

  // Sort the array of key-value pairs based on their keys
  const sortedEntries = entries.sort((a, b) => {
    return String.localeCompare(a[0], b[0]);
  });

  // Create a new JSON object from the sorted array of key-value pairs
  const sortedJsonObj = Object.fromEntries(sortedEntries);

  return sortedJsonObj;
}
```

This function takes a single argument `jsonObj`, which represents the JSON object that needs to be sorted. It then converts the JSON object into an array of key-value pairs using `Object.entries()`. This array is sorted based on the keys using `Array.prototype.sort()` with a custom comparison function `String.localeCompare()`. Finally, the sorted key-value pairs are transformed back into a JSON object using `Object.fromEntries()`.

